            "isualPath\": [\n     \"Structures/Ballista_L2\",\n     \"Structures/Ballista_L3\"\n    ],\n    \"_upgradeVisualNote\": \"WO-1046 asked whether the tower upgrade is 'just a reskin'; for this row it was not even that - maxLevel was already 3 with a two-step upgradeCost table, but there was NO upgradeVisualPath at all, so all three levels rendered the SAME borrowed wizard tower. The ladder was real in cost and stats and invisible to the player, which is the worst of both: paid for, never seen. Owner ruling 2026-08-17: 'i want it like Archer Tower - Lv2 -Lv3'. Wired to the owner-purchased Ballista_L1/L2/L3 set, mirroring tower_archer's authoring exactly. NO upgradeTexturePath: unlike the archer L3 (WO-928 defect B) each Ballista level is a SEPARATE model carrying its own basecolor, so there is no scraped-material problem to correct and a forced albedo would only override art that is already right.\",\n    \"navSurface\": \"Blocker\",\n    \"heightMul\": 0.75,\n    \"range\": 22,\n    \"damage\": 30,\n    \"fireRate\": 0.5,\n    \"canHitAir\": true,\n    \"element\": \"None\",\n    \"projectileStyle\": \"bolt\",\n    \"placement\": {\n     \"mustSitOn\": \"Ground\",\n     \"footprint\": 1.4,\n     \"noOverlap\": true,\n     \"checkAffordable\": true\n    },\n    \"_heightNote\": \"SIEGE ENGINE, not a tower silhouette \u2014 OWNER RULING 2026-08-23. It was typed Tower on the 1.2 tower cadence anchor, and STRUCTURE_ORIENTATION_FAIL flagged it 'NOT STANDING' (upright aspect 0.70 L1 / 0.94 L2, below the measured 1.2 floor). The oracle names exactly two ways to be there and they have different fixes: (a) the model is mis-oriented, or (b) the ROW is mis-classed. The owner ruled (b): a ballista is a wide machine on a carriage, so its heightMul belongs in the SIEGE-ENGINE group at 0.75 alongside tower_catapult and tower_siege_tower. \u26d4 This is a RECLASS, not a widened floor \u2014 the row stops failing because it is correctly classed. Do NOT widen the oracle's 1.2 tower floor to accommodate it, and do NOT 're-orient' the art: the model was never lying down. `type` stays Tower because that field is a ",
            "LIVE SAVE KEY and a behaviour selector (it still fires); only the height cadence moved.\"\n   },\n   \"orientation\": {\n    \"corrected\": false,\n    \"manual\": true,\n    \"euler\": [\n     0,\n     0,\n     0\n    ],\n    \"offset\": [\n     0,\n     0,\n     0\n    ],\n    \"scale\": 1,\n    \"note\": \"manual \u2014 owner ruling 2026-07-08: the model IS a ballista (renamed); Tripo fbx stands upright with the standard X-90 (supersedes the dialed (0,45,-90)). Base visual only; L2 Tower_Medieval_Big is upright polyperfect (ReskinForLevel skips base-authored orientation). AXIS-BAKE RETIREMENT 2026-08-18: the -90 X is GONE from this row because the axis conversion now lives in the MESH (bakeAxisConversion: 1 on the source FBX, set by TripoAssetPostprocessor / TripoAxisBake). Keeping it here applied the correction TWICE (baked mesh + this euler) and laid the model down. manual:true is DELIBERATELY KEPT at (0,0,0) so no auto-baker re-tips this row - the tower_ground_archer precedent. This SUPERSEDES commit f995c4706, which retired the ten -90s in Assets/OffsetForge/offsets.json - an INERT file for structures (AttachmentOffsetRegistry is keyed by hero/enemy attachment mesh ids; nothing resolves a structure id through it). The LIVE structure orientation channel is entry.orientation here, applied by StructureFactory.Create when manual==true (Assets/_Modules/Village/Catalog/StructureFactory.cs:151-158). Was [-90.0, 0.0, 0.0].\"\n   },\n   \"canHitAir\": true,\n   \"note\": \"WO-989: id renamed tower_wall_wizard->tower_ballista; alias on CatalogRegistry.Get.\",\n   \"_artNote\": \"SUPERSEDED 2026-08-17. Read as: 'the Ballista renders as WizardTower_1 because renaming the art was deferred.' That deferral lasted long enough that a row named Ballista, costing wood+iron, firing bolts, shipped to players showing a WIZARD TOWER - and the note describing the placeholder made it look accounted-for rather than broken. Resolved by owner-purchased art, not a rename: visualPrefabPath is now Structures/Ballista_L1 with a real L2/L3 ladder above it. Kept, not deleted, so nobody re-",
            "derives the WizardTower_1 path as current. HISTORY: WO-989 noted the path was GUID-stable and deferred the art.\"\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"tower_siege_tower\",\n   \"_heightNote\": \"SIEGE-ENGINE group, 0.75 (3.0 m), kept in the 2026-08-05 cadence pass. This one is also the only mustSitOn WallWalk row: it sits ON TOP of a wall, so holding it under the house line is what keeps the stacked wall-plus-engine silhouette from out-topping the 4.8 m towers.\",\n   \"displayName\": \"Sky Ballista (Anti-Air)\",\n   \"description\": \"Wall-mounted spear thrower \u2014 fires spears at flying creatures; ignores ground. The strategic counter to the sky dragon.\",\n   \"type\": \"Tower\",\n   \"kind\": \"Cell\",\n   \"visualPrefabPath\": \"Structures/Ballista\",\n   \"repo\": {\n    \"behaviorId\": \"DefenseTower\",\n    \"buildCost\": 560,\n    \"_costBasketNote\": \"WO-947 (owner economy ruling 2026-08-10): REGULAR structures cost wood + iron (\u00b1 food) and NEVER crystals; magical/ethereal structures are crystal-based. No basket ever holds wood AND iron AND crystals. This row is REGULAR by its own catalog data \u2014 displayName 'Sky Ballista (Anti-Air)', description 'Wall-mounted spear thrower', element None, projectileStyle 'bolt', and the top-level _heightCadence puts it in the SIEGE ENGINE group ('Machines, not architecture'). The former crystals (20 / 24 / 50) were folded 1:1 into IRON so the basket TOTAL and the tier-monotonic ladder are unchanged (270 / 324 / 675); only the composition moved. Numbers stay owner-tunable.\",\n    \"cost\": {\n     \"wood\": 640,\n     \"food\": 0,\n     \"iron\": 440,\n     \"crystals\": 0\n    },\n    \"maxLevel\": 3,\n    \"upgradeCost\": [\n     {\n      \"wood\": 1920,\n      \"food\": 0,\n      \"iron\": 1320,\n      \"crystals\": 0\n     },\n     {\n      \"wood\": 5600,\n      \"food\": 0,\n      \"iron\": 3850,\n      \"crystals\": 0\n     }\n    ],\n    \"navSurface\": \"Blocker\",\n    \"heightMul\": 0.75,\n    \"r